  "id": "Compound::DB01181 - Disease::DOID:2994",
  "verbalization": "Ifosfamide is linked to Germ Cell Cancer through a series of interconnected pathways that highlight its role as a cytotoxic agent. The evidence suggests that Ifosfamide, through its treatment of Testicular Cancer, which in turn is treated by Etoposide, ultimately contributes to the treatment of Germ Cell Cancer. This chain of treatment relationships underscores the involvement of Etoposide, an antineoplastic agent, in the therapeutic cascade. Additionally, the presence of Etoposide in the pathway reinforces the classification of Ifosfamide and Etoposide as heteroorganic entities, which may contribute to their shared mechanism of action. The evidence also indicates that Ifosfamide can cause Haematotoxicity, which is mediated by Etoposide, further supporting the notion of a shared biological role in the context of chemotherapy. The integration of these pathways suggests that Ifosfamide may exert its therapeutic effect through a mechanism that involves Etoposide, thereby contributing to the treatment of Germ Cell Cancer.",
